cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite both this deposit and the article it supports."
type: dataset
title: "Soil organic carbon mapping in the Motupe River watershed, northern Peru: observations, covariates, fitted models and prediction surfaces"
version: 1.1.0
# DOI-LINE
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Soil organic carbon (SOC) observations (n = 109), 13 covariate layers at 30 m,
  the fitted base learners and ensembles, the out-of-fold predictions behind the
  published accuracy metrics, and the 30 m prediction and uncertainty surfaces for
  the Motupe River watershed (Lambayeque, Peru; 3,673.66 km2, 0-3,500 m a.s.l.).
  The archive also contains the R pipeline and the two scripts that reproduce every
  number and figure of the methods post on ensemble combination. SOC ranges from
  0.42 % to 0.87 % (mean 0.649 %, SD 0.1055 %). All metrics in the post are computed
  from out-of-fold predictions under 5-fold spatial block cross-validation.
keywords:
  - soil organic carbon
  - digital soil mapping
  - ensemble machine learning
  - spatial cross-validation
  - forecast combination
  - dry forest
  - Lambayeque
  - Peru
